## Key Design Principles
1. Modular architecture
2. Simple solutions over unnecessary abstraction
3. No hard-coded model names or paths
4. No GPU assumptions
5. Models loaded on demand
6. Configuration in files, not code
7. Provider/engine interfaces independent from agent layer
8. Frontend/backend separation
9. No unrestricted system access by default
10. Destructive operations require explicit permission
11. Every major feature must be testable independently
12. Incremental implementation

## Important Constraints
- Never silently download or execute unknown binaries
- Never commit model files, secrets, or build artifacts
- Use platform-aware path handling
- Store model files outside Git repository
- Keep agent tool access permission-based
- Performance is first-class requirement for low-resource systems

## Development Guidelines
- Work in milestones, not entire system generation
- Inspect existing structure before making changes
- Read relevant documentation
- Identify dependencies first
- Implement smallest correct change
- Don't rewrite unrelated files
- Run relevant tests
- Update documentation when architecture changes
- Use small, logical git commits

## Configuration Locations
- Main config: `config/default.yaml`
- Models: `config/models.yaml`
- Permissions: `config/permissions.yaml`
- Project instructions: `.local-ai/instructions.md` or `.local-ai/config.yaml`

## CLI Commands (Planned)
Initial focus:
- `ai doctor` - System diagnostics
- `ai model list` - List installed models
- `ai model use` - Select active model
- `ai chat` - Interactive chat

Future commands:
- `ai model install/remove/info`
- `ai agent` - Agent operations
- `ai project init` - Project setup
- `ai config` - Configuration management
- `ai server start/stop` - Web server control
- `ai version` - Version information

